TNULL19 =               999999                                                  ID      = 'main    '                                                            NAME    = 'main    '                                                            COMMENT --BEGIN-ASTROPY-SERIALIZED-COLUMNS--                                    COMMENT datatype:                                                               COMMENT - name: source_id                                                       COMMENT   datatype: int64                                                       COMMENT   description: Healpix number using Nside = 4096 with the nested schem\ COMMENT e on equatorial coordinates times 2^35. The last digits of the          COMMENT     source_id are reserved for a running number that serves as a uniqu\ COMMENT e identifier per HEALPix cell. This is formed in accordance with        COMMENT     Gaia's source_id definition, but of course mock objects have no re\ COMMENT lation to any Gaia objects that may have an identical source_id.        COMMENT   meta: !!omap                                                          COMMENT   - {ucd: meta.id;meta.main}                                            COMMENT   - values:                                                             COMMENT       max: {inclusive: true, value: 6917528409165791232}                COMMENT       min: {inclusive: true, value: 3161095929857}                      COMMENT       'null': -9223372036854775808                                      COMMENT - name: ra                                                              COMMENT   unit: deg                                                             COMMENT   datatype: float64                                                     COMMENT   description: Barycentric Right Ascension in ICRS at ref_epoch         COMMENT   meta: !!omap                                                          COMMENT   - {ucd: pos.eq.ra;meta.main}                                          COMMENT - name: dec                                                             COMMENT   unit: deg                                                             COMMENT   datatype: float64                                                     COMMENT   description: Barycentric Declination in ICRS at ref_epoch             COMMENT   meta: !!omap                                                          COMMENT   - {ucd: pos.eq.dec;meta.main}                                         COMMENT - name: l                                                               COMMENT   unit: deg                                                             COMMENT   datatype: float64                                                     COMMENT   description: Galactic longitude (converted from ra, dec)              COMMENT   meta: !!omap                                                          COMMENT   - {ucd: pos.galactic.lon}                                             COMMENT - name: b                                                               COMMENT   unit: deg                                                             COMMENT   datatype: float64                                                     COMMENT   description: Galactic latitude (converted from ra, dec)               COMMENT   meta: !!omap                                                          COMMENT   - {ucd: pos.galactic.lat}                                             COMMENT - name: parallax                                                        COMMENT   unit: mas                                                             COMMENT   datatype: float32                                                     COMMENT   description: Absolute barycentric stellar parallax of the source at \ COMMENT the reference epoch ref_epoch. If looking for a distance, consider      COMMENT     joining with gdr2dist.main and using the distances from there.      COMMENT   meta: !!omap                                                          COMMENT   - {ucd: pos.parallax}                                                 COMMENT - name: parallax_error                                                  COMMENT   unit: mas                                                             COMMENT   datatype: float32                                                     COMMENT   description: Standard error of parallax                               COMMENT   meta: !!omap                                                          COMMENT   - {ucd: stat.error;pos.parallax}                                      COMMENT - name: pmra_error                                                      COMMENT   unit: mas / yr                                                        COMMENT   datatype: float32                                                     COMMENT   description: Standard error of pmra                                   COMMENT   meta: !!omap                                                          COMMENT   - {ucd: stat.error;pos.pm;pos.eq.ra}                                  COMMENT - name: pmdec_error                                                     COMMENT   unit: mas / yr                                                        COMMENT   datatype: float32                                                     COMMENT   description: Standard error of pmdec                                  COMMENT   meta: !!omap                                                          COMMENT   - {ucd: stat.error;pos.pm;pos.eq.dec}                                 COMMENT - name: radial_velocity_error                                           COMMENT   unit: km / s                                                          COMMENT   datatype: float32                                                     COMMENT   description: The radial velocity error is the error on the median to\ COMMENT  which a constant noise floor of 0.11 km/s has been added in quadratur\ COMMENT e                                                                       COMMENT     to take into account the calibration contribution.                  COMMENT   meta: !!omap                                                          COMMENT   - {ucd: stat.error;spect.dopplerVeloc}                                COMMENT - name: phot_g_mean_mag                                                 COMMENT   unit: mag                                                             COMMENT   datatype: float32                                                     COMMENT   description: Mean magnitude in the G band. This is computed from the\ COMMENT  G-band mean flux applying the magnitude zero-point in the Vega         COMMENT     scale.                                                              COMMENT   meta: !!omap                                                          COMMENT   - {ucd: phot.mag;em.opt;stat.mean}                                    COMMENT - name: phot_bp_mean_mag                                                COMMENT   unit: mag                                                             COMMENT   datatype: float32                                                     COMMENT   description: Mean magnitude in the integrated BP band. This is compu\ COMMENT ted from the BP-band mean flux applying the magnitude zero-point        COMMENT     in the Vega scale. No error is provided for this quantity as the e\ COMMENT rror distribution is only symmetric in flux space. For errors           COMMENT     small compared to the flux (less than 10%, say), the magnitude err\ COMMENT or is well approximated by 1.09*flux/flux_err.                          COMMENT   meta: !!omap                                                          COMMENT   - {ucd: phot.mag;em.opt.B}                                            COMMENT - name: phot_rp_mean_mag                                                COMMENT   unit: mag                                                             COMMENT   datatype: float32                                                     COMMENT   description: Mean magnitude in the integrated RP band. This is compu\ COMMENT ted from the RP-band mean flux applying the magnitude zero-point        COMMENT     in the Vega scale. No error is provided for this quantity as the e\ COMMENT rror distribution is only symmetric in flux space. For errors           COMMENT     small compared to the flux (less than 10%, say), the magnitude err\ COMMENT or is well approximated by 1.09*flux/flux_err.                          COMMENT   meta: !!omap                                                          COMMENT   - {ucd: phot.mag;em.opt.R}                                            COMMENT - name: phot_rvs_mean_mag                                               COMMENT   unit: mag                                                             COMMENT   datatype: float32                                                     COMMENT   description: '[GeDR3mock only] apparent magnitude of the RVS band.'   COMMENT   meta: !!omap                                                          COMMENT   - {ucd: phot.color;em.opt.I}                                          COMMENT - name: bp_rp                                                           COMMENT   unit: mag                                                             COMMENT   datatype: float32                                                     COMMENT   description: BP-RP color                                              COMMENT   meta: !!omap                                                          COMMENT   - {ucd: phot.color;em.opt.B;em.opt.R}                                 COMMENT - name: logg                                                            COMMENT   unit: log(cm/(s**2))                                                  COMMENT   datatype: float32                                                     COMMENT   description: '[GeDR3mock only] Logarithm of surface gravity.'         COMMENT   meta: !!omap                                                          COMMENT   - {ucd: phys.gravity}                                                 COMMENT - name: teff_val                                                        COMMENT   unit: K                                                               COMMENT   datatype: float32                                                     COMMENT   description: Effective temperature of the star                        COMMENT   meta: !!omap                                                          COMMENT   - {ucd: phys.temperature}                                             COMMENT - name: astrometric_params_solved                                       COMMENT   datatype: int16                                                       COMMENT   description: "This is a binary code indicating which astrometric par\ COMMENT ameters were estimated for the source. A set bit means the parameter\   COMMENT     \ was estimated. The least-significant bit represents \u03B1, the \ COMMENT next bits \u03B4, parallax, PM(RA) and PM(De). For Gaia DR2 the\        COMMENT     \ only relevant values are 31 (all five parameters solved) and 3 (\ COMMENT only positions)."                                                       COMMENT   meta: !!omap                                                          COMMENT   - {ucd: meta.code}                                                    COMMENT   - values: {'null': -1}                                                COMMENT - name: random_index                                                    COMMENT   datatype: int64                                                       COMMENT   description: Random index that can be used to deterministically sele\ COMMENT ct subsets                                                              COMMENT   meta: !!omap                                                          COMMENT   - {ucd: meta.code}                                                    COMMENT   - values: {'null': -9223372036854775808}                              